WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.968 --> 00:00:03.469
 Vince, Casey, congratulations.

00:00:03.535 --> 00:00:05.138
You guys have made it
into the third round

00:00:05.205 --> 00:00:06.372
of this competition.

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:07.974
Now, it's not going
to get any easier

00:00:08.041 --> 00:00:11.944
as we said you hoped to
recreate this iconic weapon

00:00:11.978 --> 00:00:12.679
from history--

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:19.986
the Jian.

00:00:20.052 --> 00:00:20.953
Good luck, gents.

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:22.022
We'll see you in four days.

00:00:26.025 --> 00:00:27.060
 It's day one.

00:00:27.127 --> 00:00:28.228
I'm here in Mount
Airy, Maryland,

00:00:28.294 --> 00:00:31.497
getting ready to
build the Jian sword.

00:00:31.564 --> 00:00:32.865
Here we go.

00:00:32.932 --> 00:00:33.966
It's that quick.

00:00:34.033 --> 00:00:36.536
I've decided to use ADC RB2.

00:00:36.602 --> 00:00:40.273
It's going to give it additional
toughness, more springiness.

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:42.241
Start at the tip and
work my way back.

00:00:42.308 --> 00:00:46.078
I have never made anything
as long as a Jian sword,

00:00:46.111 --> 00:00:49.215
so this is completely
new territory.

00:00:49.282 --> 00:00:50.883
Well, that's not good.

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:52.218
So I got a band.

00:00:52.285 --> 00:00:56.756
As I forge the blade, I keep
having this little ghost

00:00:56.822 --> 00:00:59.125
visiting and kinking the blade.

00:00:59.158 --> 00:01:02.428
When I get it straightened--

00:01:02.495 --> 00:01:03.263
not quite.

00:01:05.864 --> 00:01:06.632
All right.

00:01:06.699 --> 00:01:08.000
I think I'm OK.

00:01:08.033 --> 00:01:09.969
Today was pretty good, actually.

00:01:10.002 --> 00:01:12.739
Got the blade more
or less profiled,

00:01:12.805 --> 00:01:14.640
and so far it looks pretty good.

00:01:14.707 --> 00:01:17.610
I need a shower, and a
cold beer would not hurt.

00:01:22.248 --> 00:01:23.148
 So it's day one.

00:01:23.215 --> 00:01:24.651
I'm back in Oklahoma.

00:01:24.717 --> 00:01:26.752
I'm ready to get started
on this Jian sword.

00:01:26.819 --> 00:01:28.487
I'm gonna go prep my steel.

00:01:28.554 --> 00:01:32.792
I'm going to try to spice it up
a bit with a little Damascus.

00:01:32.858 --> 00:01:35.928
I'm doing 1084, and 15, and 20.

00:01:35.994 --> 00:01:37.062
I figured that would look cool.

00:01:37.129 --> 00:01:39.632
Low layer with a twist.

00:01:39.665 --> 00:01:40.767
Whoa, that's good.

00:01:40.833 --> 00:01:43.002
I've got this thing drawn
out, and as you twist it,

00:01:43.069 --> 00:01:44.403
it cools it even faster.

00:01:44.470 --> 00:01:46.772
And the more it cools down,
the harder it is to twist.

00:01:46.805 --> 00:01:48.007
So you don't want to fight it.

00:01:48.073 --> 00:01:49.875
When it tells you to
stop, you want to stop.

00:01:49.942 --> 00:01:51.210
I don't want to risk it.

00:01:51.277 --> 00:01:53.880
If it gets too cold, you
can induce stress fractures.

00:01:53.946 --> 00:01:55.314
I'm looking good.

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:56.882
I've got that twist in there,
and now I've got to square

00:01:56.949 --> 00:01:58.184
it back up and draw it out.

00:01:58.217 --> 00:02:01.488 line:7%
It's looking good, I think.

00:02:01.554 --> 00:02:02.254 line:7%
 Today's day two.

00:02:02.321 --> 00:02:03.556 line:7%
Got a good night's sleep.

00:02:03.623 --> 00:02:05.558
Hopefully I get to quench
by the end of the day.

00:02:05.624 --> 00:02:10.196
Just trying to get the
bevels established.

00:02:10.229 --> 00:02:11.497
I think that's pretty good.

00:02:11.564 --> 00:02:15.101
So I finished all my bevels,
and I'm ready to quench.

00:02:15.167 --> 00:02:17.336
I'm trying to hurry up in here.

00:02:17.402 --> 00:02:19.872
We have thunderstorms coming.

00:02:19.939 --> 00:02:24.310
With the rain, it can cause
all the oil to splatter out,

00:02:24.377 --> 00:02:25.477
and I will end up burned.

00:02:25.511 --> 00:02:27.947
So I really need
to get this done.

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:29.482
Here goes nothing.

00:02:29.549 --> 00:02:31.784
So I get the blade
to temperature.

00:02:31.851 --> 00:02:34.554
And I pull the blade out,
and it's got a slight warp.

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:37.589
I'm trying to correct it
while the blade is still hot.

00:02:37.623 --> 00:02:41.060
It's on fire, but we've
got a straight blade.

00:02:41.127 --> 00:02:42.428
I feel excited--

00:02:42.462 --> 00:02:43.562
Yes!

00:02:43.629 --> 00:02:47.133
--and I know I have a good
chance of winning this thing.

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:48.168
Perfect timing.

00:02:51.004 --> 00:02:52.738 line:0%
 So it's the
beginning of day three.

00:02:52.805 --> 00:02:53.939
I've got the guard on.

00:02:54.006 --> 00:02:55.507
I've got the handle
where I want it.

00:02:55.574 --> 00:02:57.243
I've got to get this
pommel on there.

00:02:57.309 --> 00:02:59.879
So I'm going to
grind this tang down.

00:02:59.946 --> 00:03:02.849
I've got the pretty thick
tail end of this tang here,

00:03:02.882 --> 00:03:05.251
and I'm trying to thread it.

00:03:05.285 --> 00:03:06.519
Oh, that's ugly.

00:03:06.585 --> 00:03:08.821
This thread is just not working.

00:03:08.888 --> 00:03:10.489
Oh, that's disappointing.

00:03:10.556 --> 00:03:12.291
So, I go back to the
grinder and grind it

00:03:12.357 --> 00:03:13.860
down to the next size threader.

00:03:16.595 --> 00:03:18.297
It's too thin.

00:03:18.363 --> 00:03:21.634
So I've got this dinky
threaded tang here.

00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:23.001
Cut that tang right off.

00:03:23.068 --> 00:03:25.004
This might cost me $10,000.

00:03:25.037 --> 00:03:26.539
Now there's nothing
left to thread.

00:03:26.605 --> 00:03:29.108
I've got to fit a bolt
into this position.

00:03:29.175 --> 00:03:30.310
Here goes the welding.

00:03:33.579 --> 00:03:35.348
All right, we'll
see how that works.

00:03:38.584 --> 00:03:41.187 line:0%
 Today's day four,
and we're going to put

00:03:41.253 --> 00:03:42.722 line:7%
the last few things together.

00:03:42.789 --> 00:03:44.357
Right now I'm just
tool blacking this.

00:03:44.424 --> 00:03:46.726
I chose to do gun
black for the guard.

00:03:46.793 --> 00:03:47.927
I'm pretty happy with it.

00:03:47.994 --> 00:03:51.564
And then I'm on to polishing
and sharpening the blade.

00:03:51.597 --> 00:03:54.634
I really have to be careful
now, because this is sharp.

00:03:54.701 --> 00:03:56.101
So I put the whole
thing together,

00:03:56.168 --> 00:03:58.471
and I notice that
it's a little too big.

00:03:58.537 --> 00:04:00.706
We are just over three pounds.

00:04:00.773 --> 00:04:04.910
I'm shooting for under
three pounds total weight.

00:04:04.977 --> 00:04:06.179
I start shrinking my pommel.

00:04:06.245 --> 00:04:08.214
I know I have too much metal.

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:09.549
It's too heavy, it's too big.

00:04:09.615 --> 00:04:11.350
That reduced about a
quarter of its weight.

00:04:11.416 --> 00:04:13.886
And now I've just got
to put it together.

00:04:13.952 --> 00:04:14.654
Here goes nothing.

00:04:18.725 --> 00:04:21.661
Now that everything is
together, it's finally done.

00:04:24.129 --> 00:04:26.198
 It's day four, and
I'm ready to start

00:04:26.265 --> 00:04:28.201
getting this sword together.

00:04:28.267 --> 00:04:30.203
It's looking like a sword, man.

00:04:30.269 --> 00:04:31.570
I'm going to finalize the edge.

00:04:31.603 --> 00:04:33.739
Haven't done really any
double-edged swords, actually.

00:04:33.772 --> 00:04:35.508
So a little bit challenging,
because now you've

00:04:35.574 --> 00:04:37.143
got two blades that can cut you.

00:04:37.176 --> 00:04:41.681
So I'm taking it nice and
slow, real calm and collected.

00:04:41.747 --> 00:04:44.117
The sacrifices we
make for our art.

00:04:44.183 --> 00:04:45.684
So once I get
everything assembled,

00:04:45.751 --> 00:04:47.854
I'm gonna take this thing
out here and swing it around,

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:49.555
see what I can cut up with it.

00:04:54.627 --> 00:04:59.998
Two pounds, 10 ounces of
kill-you-quick Jian sword.

00:05:00.065 --> 00:05:01.233
 All right, bladesmiths.

00:05:01.300 --> 00:05:04.503
Welcome to kill test.

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:07.840
Now, your Jian swords look
beautiful, but are they deadly?

00:05:07.907 --> 00:05:10.042
Well, to find that out,
I will take your weapon

00:05:10.075 --> 00:05:14.980
and do some slashes and thrusts
on this ballistics dummy.

00:05:15.047 --> 00:05:15.848
Vince, you're up first.

00:05:15.882 --> 00:05:16.616
Are you ready?

00:05:16.683 --> 00:05:18.384
 Give her hell.

00:05:18.451 --> 00:05:21.521
I always wanted to hear
Doug say, "It will kill,"

00:05:21.554 --> 00:05:24.490
so the anticipation
is just killing me.

00:05:24.524 --> 00:05:30.296
I want to see him get through
the test and see what he does.

00:05:30.363 --> 00:05:37.837
[impact sounds]

00:05:49.115 --> 00:05:50.282
 All right, Vince.

00:05:50.315 --> 00:05:52.651
Let's talk about your
Jian sword up here.

00:05:52.718 --> 00:05:57.022
Overall, I like the
aesthetics of this sword.

00:05:57.089 --> 00:06:01.693
Now, your handle construction
is within scale of this blade.

00:06:01.760 --> 00:06:04.196
It's comfortable when
I wrap around it.

00:06:04.262 --> 00:06:06.999
Now, your edge is razor sharp.

00:06:07.066 --> 00:06:09.702
In thrusting, it cuts
out, and when you swing

00:06:09.768 --> 00:06:12.037
you can feel the
impact of this sword.

00:06:12.104 --> 00:06:15.073
Overall, sir, it will kill.

00:06:15.140 --> 00:06:16.809
 Wanted to hear that.

00:06:16.876 --> 00:06:17.810
 Good job.

00:06:17.876 --> 00:06:19.778
 Hey, Casey, you got
the stomach for this?

00:06:19.845 --> 00:06:20.912
You're next.

00:06:20.979 --> 00:06:22.081
 I'm ready.

00:06:22.114 --> 00:06:26.218
"Forged In Fire" makes you
nervous, excited, scared,

00:06:26.284 --> 00:06:28.320
and happy all at the same time.

00:06:28.353 --> 00:06:29.521
I'm very confident in my blade.

00:06:29.588 --> 00:06:31.023
It's just, you never know.

00:06:31.090 --> 00:06:32.158
I've seen blades break.

00:06:32.191 --> 00:06:33.493
I don't want that
to happen to mine.

00:06:36.261 --> 00:06:41.801
[impact sounds]

00:06:56.448 --> 00:06:57.517
All right, Casey.

00:06:57.583 --> 00:06:59.685
Let's talk about
your Jian sword here.

00:06:59.752 --> 00:07:03.022
First up, I like the lines that
you have with your sword here,

00:07:03.089 --> 00:07:05.257
and the Damascus pattern.

00:07:05.324 --> 00:07:07.226
I can appreciate that.

00:07:07.293 --> 00:07:08.894
And now, in cutting.

00:07:08.928 --> 00:07:13.899
It was much fun just to be
able to slice over and over

00:07:13.965 --> 00:07:19.471
and over with ease with
a blade that moves.

00:07:19.538 --> 00:07:21.973
This, sir, will kill.

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:22.809
 Thank you.

00:07:26.578 --> 00:07:28.981
 Bladesmiths, welcome
to the strength test.

00:07:33.719 --> 00:07:36.321
Now to test the edge-holding
ability of your blades

00:07:36.388 --> 00:07:38.223
and the overall strength
and construction,

00:07:38.290 --> 00:07:40.526
I'm gonna take
each of your swords

00:07:40.593 --> 00:07:44.296
and smash them repeatedly
into these heavy pots.

00:07:44.330 --> 00:07:47.399
Now, I'm not really concerned
what your blades do the pots,

00:07:47.432 --> 00:07:49.001
even though it's going
to look really cool

00:07:49.068 --> 00:07:49.936
and be a lot of fun.

00:07:50.002 --> 00:07:51.236
I want to see what
the pots are going

00:07:51.303 --> 00:07:53.171
to do your blades and edges.

00:07:53.238 --> 00:07:54.273
Vince, you're up first.

00:07:54.307 --> 00:07:55.074
You ready to go?

00:07:55.141 --> 00:07:56.075
 Yes, sir.

00:07:56.142 --> 00:07:58.411
Jay picks up my blade,
and he looks excited.

00:07:58.444 --> 00:08:00.913
He's just looking
forward to smashing it.

00:08:00.979 --> 00:08:03.716
But at the same time,
if it survives Jay,

00:08:03.782 --> 00:08:06.919
I know it will survive anything.

00:08:06.985 --> 00:08:13.559
[pots shattering]

00:08:24.637 --> 00:08:26.805
Well, Vince, I've got to
tell you, it's a great blade.

00:08:26.872 --> 00:08:28.574
I mean, where I was
striking is still

00:08:28.607 --> 00:08:32.612
sharp, still straight and true.

00:08:32.678 --> 00:08:36.582
But the problem is
doing your pommel,

00:08:36.648 --> 00:08:39.651
your threads here didn't
go very far through.

00:08:39.718 --> 00:08:42.388
So the pommel broke loose.

00:08:42.455 --> 00:08:43.589
A bit of a problem.

00:08:47.026 --> 00:08:49.495
Vince, your blade has suffered
a catastrophic failure

00:08:49.561 --> 00:08:51.731
after three shots on the pots.

00:08:51.764 --> 00:08:55.134
A pommel is critical to a
one-handed weapon's retention.

00:08:55.200 --> 00:08:57.636
But that doesn't mean that
this competition is over.

00:08:57.703 --> 00:09:01.840
Casey, these are some pretty
strong terracotta pots,

00:09:01.873 --> 00:09:03.776
and you'll have to
survive three pot

00:09:03.842 --> 00:09:05.477
shots to make it out of here.

00:09:05.511 --> 00:09:06.378
 I feel ready.

00:09:06.445 --> 00:09:07.112
 All right, Jay.

00:09:07.179 --> 00:09:09.782
Are you ready?

00:09:09.848 --> 00:09:13.285
 If the pots can knock off a
pommel, they could do anything.

00:09:13.352 --> 00:09:14.487
It all comes down to this.

00:09:14.520 --> 00:09:16.121
Got a little bit of
knots in my stomach.

00:09:16.188 --> 00:09:19.392
We'll see what happens.

00:09:19.458 --> 00:09:24.564
[pots shattering]

00:09:33.138 --> 00:09:33.839
 Looks good.

00:09:38.177 --> 00:09:39.511
 Casey, congratulations.

00:09:39.578 --> 00:09:40.779
Your blade survived.

00:09:40.846 --> 00:09:45.017
Vince, unfortunately you
cannot continue testing.

00:09:45.084 --> 00:09:47.653
Please exit the forge.

00:09:47.686 --> 00:09:48.654
 I'm disappointed.

00:09:48.721 --> 00:09:49.922
I think I made a
hell of a blade.

00:09:49.989 --> 00:09:53.425
It was still sharp after
the three terracottas,

00:09:53.491 --> 00:09:56.628
but the blade needs to be 100%.

00:09:56.695 --> 00:10:00.099
Mine was 98%, and it failed.

00:10:02.335 --> 00:10:03.602
Congratulations.
- Good job, brother.

00:10:03.669 --> 00:10:04.570
 Thank you.

00:10:04.636 --> 00:10:05.738
 You put up a hell of a fight.

00:10:05.804 --> 00:10:06.939
 This is bringing
me one step closer

00:10:07.006 --> 00:10:09.675
to continue to
achieve my dreams,

00:10:09.708 --> 00:10:13.245
and I wouldn't change a thing.

00:10:13.312 --> 00:10:14.646
 Casey, congratulations.

00:10:14.713 --> 00:10:16.047
You are the "Forged
in Fire" champion,

00:10:16.114 --> 00:10:17.916
and that's a title
that comes with a check

00:10:17.983 --> 00:10:20.319
for 10,000 big ones, buddy.

00:10:20.386 --> 00:10:22.554
Congratulations.

00:10:22.621 --> 00:10:24.556
 Thank you.

00:10:24.623 --> 00:10:26.892
The deed is done, and I won.

00:10:26.959 --> 00:10:29.662
 Great steel and a great
job on that handle, too.

00:10:29.729 --> 00:10:31.830
CASEY: I've proven
to myself that I

00:10:31.897 --> 00:10:33.832
can make a damn good blade.

00:10:33.898 --> 00:10:35.334
For me, there's nothing better.

00:10:35.401 --> 00:10:38.170
[music playing]

